{"chain_id": 1315, "answer": "To reduce the risk that stakeholders become skeptical and slow to adopt AI decision-making systems when they do not understand why specific decisions were made, it has been proposed to deploy counterfactual explanation modules that automatically generate causal, irreducible counterfactual explanations for each decision (https://arxiv.org/abs/2001.07417). This is achieved through a heuristic search mechanism for minimal-cost counterfactual feature sets, wherein an algorithm efficiently finds small or cheap explanations by removing the features that most reduce the decision score per unit cost (https://arxiv.org/abs/2001.07417)."}
